          (p "Constants and procedure of the OpenGL utility library.")
          (p (b "Note:")
             " Some OpenGL functions accept pointers to buffers of various sizes (for example "
             (tt "gl:CallLists")
             "). To convert a byte- or SRFI-4 number-vector to a pointer that can be passed to the function, use "
             (tt "location")
             " or "
             (tt "make-locative")
             ". See the Chicken manual for more information."))))
   (section
    3
    "Example"
    (p "An SDL based version of the well-known \"gears\" example can be found in the file "
       (tt "sdl-gears.scm")
       " in the egg release."))
   (section
    3
    "Changelog"
    (ul (li "1.16 Removed use of " (tt "___callback"))
        (li "1.15 Removed .svn directory from wrapped egg [reported by Brandon Van Every]")
        (li "1.14 Fixed bug in .setup script [Thanks to Brandon van Every]")
        (li "1.13 Moved GLUT functionality into a separate egg ("
            (int-link "glut")
            ")")
        (li "1.12 Adapted to externalized " (tt "easyffi") " extension")
        (li "1.11 Added Cygwin specific patches by Dominique Boucher")
        (li "1.10 Should now properly build on Mac OS X")
        (li "1.9 Supports now OpenGL 1.2+ functions, ported to Windows [Thanks to Ashley Bone]")
        (li "1.8 Henrik Tramberend kindly added support for Mac OS X")
        (li "1.7 Fixed definition of " (tt "GLU_TESS_MAX_COORD"))
        (li "1.6 Adapted to new setup scheme.")
        (li "1.5 Peter Wang contributed several missing definitions.")
        (li "1.4 Added support for the new "
            (tt "byte")
            " and "
            (tt "unsigned-byte")
            " types.")
        (li "1.3 Added "
            (tt "-lXmu")
            " to link-command for "
            (tt "(opengl glut)")
            " extension [Thanks to Matthias Heiler]")
        (li "1.2 Added various missing definitions, character-drawing procedures accept chars instead of integers, callbacks work for multiple windows.")
        (li "1.1 Fixed bug in name-substitution declarations [Thanks to Daniel B. Faken]")
        (li "1.0 Initial release")))
